# Target by expected value, then prove the save rate
## Executive summary

- Same {{ budget.base | usd }} budget: {{ headline.delta_vs_risk | signed_usd }} expected versus calling the riskiest customers
- Who: fibre customers on monthly contracts with high bills; not low-risk or low-bill customers
- Budget: about {{ scaled.recommended_budget | usd }} for the base; stop where the next step returns under {{ recommendation.hurdle_marginal_roi | pct(0) }}
- Who to target is robust; how much an offer saves ({{ default_offer.save_rate | pct(0) }} assumed) is not
- Ask: one pilot wave, half held out, about {{ pilot.wave_cost | usd }} of offers and contacts

Notes: If management remembers one slide, it is this one. The targeting gain holds in {{ mc.base_vs_risk.prob_gain | pct(0) }} of assumption draws; the save rate is the open question, which is why the ask is a pilot and not a roll-out.

