# Churn puts {{ value_at_risk.expected_scaled | usd }} of margin at risk
## Today's rule calls the riskiest customers, whatever they are worth
![](../figures/eda_drivers.png)

- {{ data.churn_rate | pct }} of customers churn; monthly-contract, new, fibre and e-cheque customers most
- The budget covers an offer for {{ budget.share | pct(0) }} of customers
- Every offer costs money, even when the customer would have stayed
- Owner: Head of Retention; Finance approves budget; Legal/DPO approves contact

Notes: {{ value_at_risk.expected_scaled | usd }} is twelve months of expected margin lost to churn across {{ scaled.base_population | num }} customers ({{ value_at_risk.expected | usd }} on the {{ data.splits.test | num }} test customers). The question is not who will leave but where an offer pays back. Our KPIs: expected net value, ROI, customers contacted, precision among contacted and coverage of high-risk, high-value customers.

