# Offer only where expected value beats the cost
## Expected value = churn probability x save rate x customer value - (offer + contact cost)

- Contact only customers with positive expected value
- An optimiser picks customers and one offer each within budget, at most {{ cfg.campaign.max_contact_share | pct(0) }} contacted
- Four offers with eligibility rules: bill credit, contract upgrade, service bundle, loyalty reward
- Every cost and save rate is a visible, sourced assumption

Notes: Worked example: a customer paying 70 dollars a month is worth about {{ worked_example.value | usd }} over a year of margin; at 60% risk the standard offer is worth {{ worked_example.ev | usd(2) }} net. The save rate is the share of would-be leavers an offer keeps; we assume {{ default_offer.save_rate | pct(0) }}, below the 30% common in the literature.

