# Spend about {{ scaled.recommended_budget | usd }} - then stop
![](../figures/profit_curve.png)

- Each extra step reaches customers with less expected value
- Keep steps that return at least {{ recommendation.hurdle_marginal_roi | pct(0) }} (set on validation): {{ budget.recommended_per_base_customer | usd(2) }} per customer
- Test customers: {{ recommended.selected_count | num }} offers, {{ recommended.cost | usd }}, net {{ recommended.expected_net_value | usd }} (ROI {{ recommended.roi | pct(0) }})
- Beyond {{ curve.positive_ev_share | pct(0) }} of customers nobody is worth an offer

Notes: The x-axis is the budget expressed as the share of customers the standard offer could reach. The recommended budget is about {{ (recommended.cost / budget.base) | num(1) }} times today's; it is only worth committing once the pilot confirms the save rate.

