# Who to target is robust; how much an offer saves is not
![](../figures/monte_carlo.png)

- Break-even save rate: {{ be.break_even_default_save_rate | pct }} (base list), {{ rbe | pct }} (recommended); assumed {{ default_offer.save_rate | pct(0) }}
- All assumptions uncertain: the recommended list loses money in {{ mc.recommended.prob_loss | pct(0) }} of draws
- Beats risk-only in {{ mc.base_vs_risk.prob_gain | pct(0) }} of draws
- Only {{ reasons.addressable_share | pct(0) }} of churners left for price or a competitor's offer

Notes: {{ monte_carlo.draws | num }} draws, every register assumption at once. {{ monte_carlo.drivers[0].label }} and {{ monte_carlo.drivers[1].label | lower }} drive most of the spread. If offers only reach churners who left for price or a competitor, a {{ default_offer.save_rate | pct(0) }} save rate means keeping {{ (default_offer.save_rate / reasons.addressable_share) | pct(0) }} of them: ambitious. Below {{ be.minimum_viable_save_rate | pct }} nobody is worth contacting.

