# The pilot measures what we assumed
- {{ pilot.list_size_per_wave | num }} customers: {{ pilot.arm_size_per_wave | num }} offered, {{ pilot.arm_size_per_wave | num }} held out at random
- Save rate = 1 - churn of offered / churn of held out, after {{ pilot.outcome_window_days }} days
- One wave detects a save rate of about {{ pilot.minimum_detectable_save_rate_one_wave | pct(0) }}; break-even is {{ rbe | pct }}
- Cost about {{ pilot.wave_cost | usd }}; expected net value of the offered half {{ pilot.wave_expected_net | usd }}
- Decision about {{ pilot.weeks_to_decision }} weeks after approval: set-up, outcome window, read-out

Notes: Randomising inside the target list gives the causal effect the data cannot. The price of learning is the value forgone on the held-out half, about {{ pilot.wave_expected_net | usd }}. Measured save rates replace the assumptions and the whole analysis re-runs.

